invariant: INV-28
file: src/tcp_nonblocking.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_tcp_init takes a configuration that sets cfg.send, which no call
  of the transport calls, so a caller that set one believes its records
  leave through it and sends nothing. tcp_nonblocking.h refuses it at
  configuration time (docs/decisions.md 248).

--- old
    if (!hspost_present_ticket(&r->t.cfg) || !tlsi_config_ok(&r->t.cfg) || cfg->send != NULL ||
        cfg->recv != NULL) {
--- new
    if (!hspost_present_ticket(&r->t.cfg) || !tlsi_config_ok(&r->t.cfg) || cfg->recv != NULL) {
